---
import BaseLayout from "../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro";

const title = "Credit Card Payoff Order (Which balance first?)";
const description =
  "Choose a payoff order based on APR, balance size, and motivation. Educational use only.";

const lastUpdated = "2026-02-08";
---
<BaseLayout title={title} description={description} canonicalPath="/guides/credit-card-payoff-order" lastUpdated={lastUpdated}>
  <section class="card hero">
    <span class="pill">Guide</span>
    <nav class="breadcrumbs" aria-label="Breadcrumb">
      <a href="/">Home</a>
      <span aria-hidden="true">/</span>
      <a href="/guides">Guides</a>
      <span aria-hidden="true">/</span>
      <span aria-current="page">Payoff order</span>
    </nav>
    <h1>Credit card payoff order</h1>
    <p>
      There are two common payoff orders: highest APR first (avalanche) and smallest balance first (snowball). This guide
      helps you choose based on cost and motivation.
    </p>
    <div class="btn-row">
      <a class="btn btn-primary" href="/calculators/debt-avalanche-calculator">Debt avalanche calculator</a>
      <a class="btn" href="/calculators/debt-snowball-calculator">Debt snowball calculator</a>
      <a class="btn" href="/topics/credit-cards">Credit cards topic</a>
    </div>
  </section>
  <section class="card section prose" style="margin-top:18px">
    <h2 style="margin-top:0">Credit card inputs to verify</h2>
    <ul class="muted" style="margin:10px 0 0; padding-left:18px">
      <li>Current balance, APR, and any promo end date.</li>
      <li>Minimum payment rule or fixed payment amount.</li>
      <li>Fees or new purchases that affect the balance.</li>
      <li>Statement cycle dates and posting timing.</li>
    </ul>
  </section>

  <section class="card section prose" style="margin-top:18px">
    <h2 style="margin-top:0">Two common strategies</h2>
    <ul class="muted" style="margin:10px 0 0; padding-left:18px">
      <li><strong>Avalanche:</strong> pay highest APR first to minimize interest.</li>
      <li><strong>Snowball:</strong> pay smallest balance first for quick wins.</li>
    </ul>
  </section>

  <section class="card section prose" style="margin-top:18px">
    <h2 style="margin-top:0">How to decide</h2>
    <ul class="muted" style="margin:10px 0 0; padding-left:18px">
      <li>If cost is the main goal, use avalanche.</li>
      <li>If staying consistent is the main goal, snowball can help.</li>
      <li>Run both calculators to compare timelines and interest.</li>
    </ul>
  </section>

  <section class="card section prose" style="margin-top:18px">
    <h2 style="margin-top:0">Numbers to line up first</h2>
    <ul class="muted" style="margin:10px 0 0; padding-left:18px">
      <li>Balance, APR, and minimum payment for each card.</li>
      <li>Total monthly extra you can add beyond minimums.</li>
      <li>Any promo APR end dates.</li>
      <li>Whether any card has a penalty APR risk.</li>
    </ul>
  </section>

  <section class="card section prose" style="margin-top:18px">
    <h2 style="margin-top:0">Decision checklist</h2>
    <ul class="muted" style="margin:10px 0 0; padding-left:18px">
      <li>List balances by APR and minimum payment.</li>
      <li>Choose a fixed monthly extra you can sustain.</li>
      <li>Pick a strategy and commit for at least 3 to 6 months.</li>
      <li>Re-rank if promo APRs expire or rates increase.</li>
    </ul>
  </section>

  <section class="card section prose" style="margin-top:18px">
    <h2 style="margin-top:0">Tie-breakers</h2>
    <ul class="muted" style="margin:10px 0 0; padding-left:18px">
      <li>Pay off balances with penalty APR risk first.</li>
      <li>Clear small balances to simplify autopay management.</li>
      <li>Protect cash flow by keeping a small reserve.</li>
      <li>Favor cards with fees or promotions ending soon.</li>
    </ul>
  </section>

  <section class="card section prose" style="margin-top:18px">
    <h2 style="margin-top:0">Execution steps</h2>
    <ul class="muted" style="margin:10px 0 0; padding-left:18px">
      <li>Set minimum payments on autopay for every card.</li>
      <li>Send the full extra amount to the top-priority card.</li>
      <li>Reallocate the freed payment after each payoff.</li>
    </ul>
  </section>

  <section class="card section prose" style="margin-top:18px">
    <h2 style="margin-top:0">Common mistakes</h2>
    <ul class="muted" style="margin:10px 0 0; padding-left:18px">
      <li>Ignoring minimum payment rules in the plan.</li>
      <li>Adding new purchases while trying to pay off balances.</li>
      <li>Switching strategies too often without a clear reason.</li>
    </ul>
  </section>

  <section class="grid" style="margin-top:18px">
    <div class="card section prose col-6">
      <h2 style="margin-top:0">Related tools</h2>
      <ul class="muted" style="margin:10px 0 0; padding-left:18px">
        <li><a href="/calculators/debt-avalanche-calculator">Debt avalanche</a></li>
        <li><a href="/calculators/debt-snowball-calculator">Debt snowball</a></li>
      </ul>
    </div>
    <div class="card section prose col-6">
      <h2 style="margin-top:0">Related guides</h2>
      <ul class="muted" style="margin:10px 0 0; padding-left:18px">
        <li><a href="/guides/debt-snowball-vs-avalanche">Debt snowball vs avalanche</a></li>
        <li><a href="/guides/credit-card-payoff-strategy">Credit card payoff strategy</a></li>
      </ul>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="card section prose" style="margin-top:18px">
    <h2 style="margin-top:0">FAQ</h2>
    <h3 style="margin:12px 0 0">Can I combine strategies?</h3>
    <p class="muted" style="margin:8px 0 0">
      You can prioritize a high APR balance first, then switch to snowball for motivation. Just keep the plan consistent.
    </p>
    <h3 style="margin:12px 0 0">Does payoff order matter with one balance?</h3>
    <p class="muted" style="margin:8px 0 0">
      No. Order only matters when you have multiple balances.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section class="card section prose" style="margin-top:18px">
    <h2 style="margin-top:0">Next steps</h2>
    <div class="btn-row" style="margin-top:10px">
      <a class="btn btn-primary" href="/calculators/debt-avalanche-calculator">Try avalanche</a>
      <a class="btn" href="/calculators/debt-snowball-calculator">Try snowball</a>
      <a class="btn" href="/topics/credit-cards">Credit cards topic</a>
    </div>
    <p class="muted" style="margin:12px 0 0">Educational use only. Not financial advice.</p>
    <p class="muted" style="margin:12px 0 0; font-size:13px">Last updated: 2026-02-08</p>
  </section>
</BaseLayout>




